---
title: "The /goal loop: what the user sees"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: idle
    lg1: done
    lg2: stopped
    lg3: running
  }
  class lg0 tan
  class lg1 blue
  class lg2 orange
  class lg3 purple
  s0: No goal
  s1: Working on a cycle
  s2: Goal stopped
  s3: Goal paused
  s4: Goal active, idle
  s5: Goal complete
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: you set a goal or you set a goal while a turn ran
  s1 --> s2: you press Esc or a cycle ends and the loop decides
  s1 --> s0: you clear the goal
  s1 --> s3: you pause the goal
  s2 --> s0: you clear the goal
  s2 --> s3: you pause the goal
  s3 --> s2: you resume, and the budget is spent
  s3 --> s0: you clear the goal
  s3 --> s1: you set a goal or you set a goal while a turn ran
  s1 --> s4: a turn ends that the loop did not start or a turn ends after you replaced its prompt
  s1 --> s5: a cycle ends and the loop decides
  s4 --> s1: you send an ordinary prompt
  s4 --> s2: you press Esc
  s4 --> s0: you clear the goal
  s4 --> s3: you pause the goal
  s2 --> s5: you resume a goal that was already met
  s3 --> s5: you resume a goal that was already met
  s5 --> s0: you clear the goal
  s5 --> s1: you set a goal while a turn ran or you set a goal
  class s0 tan
  class s1 purple
  class s2 orange
  class s3 orange
  class s4 purple
  class s5 blue
